{"uid":"8c01038952e018c7","name":"test_the_contradictory_pair_converges_but_only_one_order_is_an_anomaly[succeeded-then-canceled]","fullName":"tests.webhook.test_ordering#test_the_contradictory_pair_converges_but_only_one_order_is_an_anomaly","time":{"start":1787290223141,"stop":1787290223154,"duration":13},"description":"D-014, and the one place where order changes something visible.\n\nsucceeded outranks canceled, so both orders end at succeeded and the state\nis order independent as everywhere else. What differs is legality: arriving\nat succeeded *out of* canceled is a transition the table calls impossible,\nso it is recorded as an anomaly. The reverse order never leaves canceled at\nall, because canceled cannot outrank succeeded, so nothing is flagged.\n\nThis asymmetry is the whole reason D-014 ranks succeeded above canceled.\nRank canceled higher instead and the contradiction is silently absorbed,\nthe illegal transition machinery becomes dead code, and a mapping bug in\nour own receiver passes unnoticed.\n","descriptionHtml":"<p>D-014, and the one place where order changes something visible.</p>\n<p>succeeded outranks canceled, so both orders end at succeeded and the state<br />\nis order independent as everywhere else. What differs is legality: arriving<br />\nat succeeded <em>out of</em> canceled is a transition the table calls impossible,<br />\nso it is recorded as an anomaly. The reverse order never leaves canceled at<br />\nall, because canceled cannot outrank succeeded, so nothing is flagged.</p>\n<p>This asymmetry is the whole reason D-014 ranks succeeded above canceled.<br />\nRank canceled higher instead and the contradiction is silently absorbed,<br />\nthe illegal transition machinery becomes dead code, and a mapping bug in<br />\nour own receiver passes unnoticed.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"base_url","time":{"st